you would have to move either move to amend uh by deleting them from the

01:15:48.830 --> 01:15:52.120
main motion or you could move to divide.

01:15:54.270 --> 01:15:55.550
Which is the easiest?

01:15:55.950 --> 01:15:58.100
Well, I, I don't know if ease is.

01:15:59.250 --> 01:16:01.110
Uh, you know, I think they're both.

01:16:02.460 --> 01:16:03.180
Division.

01:16:03.620 --> 01:16:04.090
Division.

01:16:04.500 --> 01:16:04.810
OK.

01:16:06.600 --> 01:16:12.390
So I um moved to put an amendment out that we divide these and vote on them.

01:16:17.050 --> 01:16:19.160
And I don't want anybody to take it personal,

01:16:19.490 --> 01:16:19.870
but.

01:16:21.260 --> 01:16:23.670
In the past I supported you, Mayor Battle,

01:16:24.020 --> 01:16:27.920
on some of your appointments that I felt people were not the best qualified,

01:16:28.060 --> 01:16:32.840
but because I was new on the council, everyone said I would come in fighting,

01:16:32.980 --> 01:16:38.850
so I came in trying to compromise, but that compromise that I did at that

01:16:38.850 --> 01:16:43.330
time still sits heavy on my chest, and I don't want any more of your appointments

01:16:43.330 --> 01:16:44.930
to sit heavy on my chest.

01:16:45.900 --> 01:16:47.030
And it's not personal.

01:16:47.590 --> 01:16:52.880
So just, just to, just to clarify, your amendment is to divide for separate

01:16:52.880 --> 01:16:56.780
consideration, um, each of for each position,

01:16:57.540 --> 01:16:59.130
and I believe the second was from Mr.

01:16:59.310 --> 01:16:59.530
Mayor.

01:16:59.620 --> 01:17:02.270
That would require a second, and that has been received,

01:17:02.300 --> 01:17:05.660
and then it has to be voted upon by the members and,

01:17:05.740 --> 01:17:08.890
and has to be approved by a majority of members.

01:17:09.170 --> 01:17:14.600
All in favor of, uh, separate consideration for each position.

01:17:15.180 --> 01:17:18.180
Um, please indicate by saying aye, aye.

01:17:18.740 --> 01:17:20.530
Any, any opposed?

01:17:20.710 --> 01:17:24.750
I'll, uh, I'll vote aye as a courtesy to my fellow council members.

01:17:24.980 --> 01:17:28.380
I really appreciate that because I, I don't understand why anybody would

01:17:28.380 --> 01:17:33.610
vote against us having an opportunity as a council member to vote individually.

01:17:33.860 --> 01:17:36.330
If one of my council members asked me right now,

01:17:36.420 --> 01:17:37.890
Michelle, can we vote separately?

01:17:38.020 --> 01:17:38.930
Absolutely.

01:17:39.780 --> 01:17:41.050
Can we finish the vote, please?

01:17:41.340 --> 01:17:43.020
So we have, uh, uh.

01:17:43.700 --> 01:17:45.300
All any opposed?

01:17:46.600 --> 01:17:46.890
No.

01:17:47.080 --> 01:17:48.070
The record shows Mr.

01:17:48.200 --> 01:17:51.510
Little has voted in opposition, so the amendment is approved.

01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:53.110
So now we will proceed.

01:17:53.360 --> 01:17:55.030
Can we continue discussion?

01:17:56.830 --> 01:18:00.560
Um, well, yes, but we're going to be, uh,

01:18:00.780 --> 01:18:03.860
taking each position separately for consideration.

01:18:07.170 --> 01:18:13.760
So Let me pull it up where it is, or do you have them here?

01:18:14.760 --> 01:18:15.390
May I use that?

01:18:15.640 --> 01:18:15.990
Thank you.

01:18:17.520 --> 01:18:18.510
Then Mr.

01:18:18.640 --> 01:18:20.420
Riley, you're going to have to guide us through this.

01:18:21.480 --> 01:18:23.760
We will then consider each.

01:18:25.460 --> 01:18:26.010
We will vote.

01:18:26.140 --> 01:18:26.970
Is this correct?

01:18:27.070 --> 01:18:30.130
We will vote to approve each position.

01:18:30.460 --> 01:18:32.680
We would vote to approve each individual,

01:18:32.780 --> 01:18:37.050
each position individually since the motion to divide has been made and

01:18:37.050 --> 01:18:41.320
approved, uh, as to each individual candidate.

01:18:42.300 --> 01:18:42.770
OK.

01:18:43.150 --> 01:18:44.930
We'll begin with Kathy Martin.

01:18:45.140 --> 01:18:48.490
Current job title is Director of City Engineering.

01:18:49.670 --> 01:18:50.280
Move to approve.

01:18:50.430 --> 01:18:52.060
Second motion from Mr.

01:18:52.460 --> 01:18:53.530
Little to approve.

01:18:53.670 --> 01:18:54.300
Second from Mr.

01:18:54.470 --> 01:18:54.820
Kling.

01:18:54.950 --> 01:18:56.060
Is there any discussion?

01:18:56.270 --> 01:18:57.100
Yes, Mr.

01:18:57.270 --> 01:18:57.780
Meredith.

01:19:00.510 --> 01:19:06.450
I definitely, uh, Respect Ms.

01:19:06.580 --> 01:19:06.980
Martin.

01:19:07.050 --> 01:19:10.330
I think she has done an absolutely phenomenal job,

01:19:10.780 --> 01:19:15.240
um, as chief engineer, um, or city engineer,

01:19:15.530 --> 01:19:21.230
um, I think that, um, she actually is qualified,

01:19:21.620 --> 01:19:23.360
uh, to make this jump.

01:19:24.020 --> 01:19:26.700
However, I think the jump's completely unnecessary.

01:19:26.780 --> 01:19:30.220
Frankly, I think this whole reorganization is unnecessary.

01:19:30.700 --> 01:19:33.810
Um, I think it smacks of cronyism.

01:19:34.690 --> 01:19:39.230
And in an era where we've been told time and time again,

01:19:39.770 --> 01:19:41.560
budget's tight, budget's tight.

01:19:42.570 --> 01:19:47.320
Well, this is not something that's done in the middle of a tight budget.

01:19:48.140 --> 01:19:52.330
You So many good organizations.

01:19:53.220 --> 01:19:57.240
have come to this city and asked for appropriations to help them carry out

01:19:57.300 --> 01:19:59.750
their work, their service work.

01:20:00.100 --> 01:20:02.750
Again, leadership's not born of power.

01:20:03.140 --> 01:20:04.490
It's born of service.

01:20:05.660 --> 01:20:17.670
And to thumb your nose at service organizations to provide Huge salary increases

01:20:18.210 --> 01:20:19.640
to a handful of people.

01:20:20.840 --> 01:20:24.490
is not what's done at a time of a very tight budget.

01:20:25.830 --> 01:20:29.900
Again Has nothing to do with Miss Martin.

01:20:30.840 --> 01:20:36.590
She is absolutely qualified for this new position.

01:20:37.440 --> 01:20:38.830
However, I think the new position.

01:20:39.550 --> 01:20:40.810
Should not have been created.

01:20:42.050 --> 01:20:45.250
And I have, like Ms.

01:20:45.380 --> 01:20:47.200
Watkins, heartburn.

01:20:48.250 --> 01:20:52.640
Over the fact that it was created at a time when there's a tight budget.

01:20:54.310 --> 01:20:56.580
No, um, I'm sorry.

01:20:57.750 --> 01:20:59.060
Um, again, Ms.

01:20:59.180 --> 01:21:01.680
Martin is qualified.

01:21:01.990 --> 01:21:03.290
That's not an issue.

01:21:03.630 --> 01:21:04.300
That's not.

01:21:05.900 --> 01:21:07.170
An argument for this.

01:21:08.610 --> 01:21:13.560
This position is irrelevant, should not be created at all.

01:21:14.960 --> 01:21:15.910
That's, that's all.

01:21:16.730 --> 01:21:17.820
Any further comments, Mr.

01:21:17.930 --> 01:21:18.470
Meredith?

01:21:19.030 --> 01:21:19.320
No, ma'am.

01:21:19.440 --> 01:21:21.590
Are there any other comments regarding, uh,

01:21:21.850 --> 01:21:22.020
Ms.

01:21:22.150 --> 01:21:27.300
Martin, Cathy Martin, uh, being appointed as senior director of engineering?

01:21:27.390 --> 01:21:29.630
As far as the position and the necessity of it,

01:21:29.790 --> 01:21:32.580
Mayor Battle, we have had the same, uh, the same,

01:21:32.750 --> 01:21:35.250
same government, same, same form of government that,

01:21:35.390 --> 01:21:40.300
uh, we had in the 1980s is the same form that we had until last meeting

01:21:40.300 --> 01:21:42.300
when we voted to reorganize.

01:21:42.730 --> 01:21:46.680
We voted to reorganize and the council voted to reorganize after the council

01:21:46.680 --> 01:21:47.730
vote to reorganize.

01:21:48.210 --> 01:21:52.520
It's my job to put the best people I can in the positions that are that

01:21:52.520 --> 01:21:56.480
are there and, um, I could not think of anybody any better than Ms.

01:21:56.560 --> 01:21:56.960
Martin.

01:21:57.430 --> 01:22:00.930
Uh, to kind of fill the space, uh, that Shane Davis was in,

01:22:01.270 --> 01:22:04.620
uh, for years and years, and she's working on roads every day.

01:22:04.750 --> 01:22:06.420
She's working on Bob Wade Lane.

01:22:06.470 --> 01:22:10.450
She's working on, uh, the road systems coming in,

01:22:10.470 --> 01:22:14.140
the resolute Way, all those road systems that are coming in.

01:22:14.230 --> 01:22:18.420
It's gonna take someone who is a senior engineer who will work with our

01:22:18.420 --> 01:22:21.050
engineering department and work with our planning department,

01:22:21.190 --> 01:22:24.450
work with other departments to make sure that we can continue to grow,

01:22:24.750 --> 01:22:25.220
uh.

01:22:25.640 --> 01:22:29.100
You know, as, as we grow, we have to also grow our infrastructure,

01:22:29.120 --> 01:22:31.210
and these are the people that make it happen.

01:22:31.560 --> 01:22:34.070
I think they're, uh, they're the people that we need to have.

01:22:35.380 --> 01:22:37.530
And again, it, it's not.

01:22:38.710 --> 01:22:40.850
An issue of her qualification.

01:22:42.300 --> 01:22:46.730
You are taking the time of a tight budget and you're doubling shame.

01:22:47.020 --> 01:22:50.700
I mean, It's not like Shane worked for $50,000 a year.

01:22:51.840 --> 01:22:55.150
You worked for over $200,000 a year and you just,

01:22:55.320 --> 01:23:01.210
poof, made another $200,000 a year job materialize out of nowhere.

01:23:02.900 --> 01:23:09.970
And as you said, it's short lived, so let's not reap all of these benefits

01:23:09.970 --> 01:23:11.050
of Ms.

01:23:11.180 --> 01:23:13.650
Martin's leadership when she's not gonna be around.

01:23:15.300 --> 01:23:16.690
It's the next person.

01:23:17.410 --> 01:23:18.630
That's problematic.

01:23:18.850 --> 01:23:19.320
It's not Ms.

01:23:19.410 --> 01:23:19.870
Martin.

01:23:20.040 --> 01:23:21.360
I said that to begin with.

01:23:21.570 --> 01:23:23.220
She is more than qualified.

01:23:23.590 --> 01:23:24.480
Absolutely.

01:23:24.610 --> 01:23:28.240
It's the person that's gonna replace her on January 1,

01:23:28.330 --> 01:23:29.320
2027.

01:23:30.110 --> 01:23:32.120
Who's gonna be unqualified.

01:23:34.180 --> 01:23:36.370
And the person who replaced her on January 1st,

01:23:36.420 --> 01:23:39.730
who we don't know who that is, that will be a person that council will have

01:23:39.730 --> 01:23:43.390
to approve coming into space, coming into working in that space.

01:23:43.820 --> 01:23:48.850
Um, council approved the, uh, reorganization at last meeting.

01:23:49.310 --> 01:23:53.290
And after the after the reorganization we were gonna put people in place

01:23:53.310 --> 01:23:55.740
who can do the job and do a great job of it.

01:23:55.870 --> 01:23:59.460
I have no qualms at putting Cathy Martin in that spot.

01:24:00.750 --> 01:24:03.210
Neither do I, but that's not the point.

01:24:03.470 --> 01:24:05.090
The point is good governance.

01:24:05.270 --> 01:24:06.500
This is not good governance.

01:24:06.590 --> 01:24:09.140
You said we've had the same government since whenever.

01:24:09.470 --> 01:24:11.100
Well, it's worked since forever.

01:24:11.200 --> 01:24:13.700
There's no need to change it now.

01:24:15.400 --> 01:24:19.380
There just isn't, and Again, we started with Ms.

01:24:19.510 --> 01:24:22.780
Martin, who is probably arguably the best qualified person.

01:24:23.540 --> 01:24:26.090
So it's not a matter of her not being qualified.

01:24:26.300 --> 01:24:30.610
It's a matter of where's all this money coming from when you said we had

01:24:30.610 --> 01:24:33.260
a tight budget and we couldn't give.

01:24:34.550 --> 01:24:41.630
Deserving organizations that are providing services to the least among us.

01:24:42.350 --> 01:24:45.450
But yet you miraculously find money for this.

01:24:45.710 --> 01:24:50.010
And yes, this council approved your reorganization,

01:24:50.310 --> 01:24:51.700
but it was not unanimous.

01:24:52.590 --> 01:24:53.470
At all.

01:24:53.950 --> 01:24:57.580
So yeah, you got 3 votes, but you didn't get 5.

01:25:00.680 --> 01:25:02.100
Are there any other comments?

01:25:02.620 --> 01:25:07.510
All in favor of, uh, the appointment of Cathy Martin to the senior director

01:25:07.510 --> 01:25:08.190
